          <h2>Overview</h2>
          <p>
            The <strong>CPU scheduler</strong> selects which process in the ready queue gets to run next.
            Scheduling is central to multiprogramming — it maximizes CPU utilization and ensures fair,
            responsive execution across concurrent processes.
          </p>
          <div class="callout">
            <span class="callout-title">Key Distinction</span>
            <p><em>Scheduling</em> decides <strong>which</strong> process runs. <em>Dispatching</em> is the mechanism
